2903: /// Wraps a [_BlockRenderer] so that the underlying block widget (and its
2904: /// [_TextSelectionSurface] children, geometry registration, and text-layout
2905: /// cache) stay mounted even when scrolled out of the viewport — but only when
2906: /// [keepAlive] is true. Used to keep the caret block and selection endpoints
2907: /// alive under editor virtualisation, so the caret and selection
2908: /// highlight always paint and the geometry registry always knows their box.
2909: ///
2910: /// Also drives incremental rebuild: a block is only re-rendered when its
2911: /// content changed ([blockChanged]) *or* when the selection / caret / IME
2912: /// composition touches it. A pure caret move inside a different block leaves
2913: /// this block's cached child intact, avoiding the inline-span rebuild that
2914: /// would otherwise run for every block on every keystroke.
